<div class="analytics-card"><p class="eyebrow">SAFE DEFAULTS / PROVIDER DISABLED</p><h1>Experiment Configuration</h1><p>Every run uses synthetic data. AI runs require separately configured credentials, reviewed prices, model verification and explicit owner opt-in. Creating a run never enables paid requests.</p><div class="configuration-grid"><label>Experiment name<input id="new-label" value="Local Genesis experiment" maxlength="120"></label><label>Population<select id="new-mode"><option>GA_ONLY</option><option>RANDOM_SEARCH</option><option>GA_HAIKU</option></select></label><label>Seed<input id="new-seed" type="number" min="1" max="2147483646" value="42"></label><label>Population size<input id="new-size" type="number" min="4" max="100" value="12"></label><label>Generations<input id="new-generations" type="number" min="1" max="1000" value="5"></label></div><button id="create-experiment" type="button">Create and start experiment</button><p id="create-status" role="status"></p><p>Default operators: tournament size 3, mutation 0.25, crossover 0.75, two elites. Database owners can configure supported parameters before initialization. A Node/Playwright worker supplies real browser observations; DBMS_SCHEDULER advances ready generations.</p></div>
```
